[32m+[m[32m# cpp-rust-performance-lab[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA reproducible research project for studying equivalent C++ and Rust implementations, beginning with small CPU and memory primitives and progressing toward selected low-latency trading-system components.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Goals[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Build disciplined performance-engineering practice through controlled experiments.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Produce results and methodology suitable for GitHub, a résumé, and technical publications.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Develop foundations that could inform a reusable performance-analysis service.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Document what is measured, how it is measured, and the limits of each conclusion.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Comparison principles[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Treat C++ and Rust as engineering tools, not competitors in a language contest.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Compare equivalent workloads, inputs, semantics, and correctness checks.[m
[32m+[m[32m- State compiler, operating-system, machine, build, and runtime configuration with every result.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Investigate generated code and measurement validity before drawing conclusions.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Avoid claims that either language is inherently faster.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Planned progression[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. CPU and memory primitives: sums, branches, dependency chains, and pointer chasing.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. Data-structure and concurrency primitives: queues, event dispatch, and memory pools.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Trading-oriented components: market-data processing, order books, risk checks, and simplified execution pipelines.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Environment and status[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe current development environment is **Ubuntu 26.04 under WSL2**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mInitial results will be machine-, compiler-, operating-system-, and configuration-specific; they are not general language-performance claims.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCurrent status: **repository bootstrap and benchmark methodology design**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Layout[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `specs/` — workload definitions and measurement methodology.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `cpp/` — future C++ implementations.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `rust/` — future Rust implementations.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `scripts/` — future reproducibility and analysis helpers.[m
